    "odia": "ତାଳ ପିଠା",
    "lead": "A golden slice and a browned edge. Follow ripe palm fruit into one of Odisha’s seasonal food stories.",
    "hero": "tala-pitha",
    "save_id": "food:tala-pitha",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "taste",
        "title": "Begin with the cut slice",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Look at the colour inside the crust. The photograph shows tala poda pitha: one answer to what a cook can make with ripe palm fruit.",
            "source_ids": [
              "photo-tala-pitha"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          },
          {
            "text": "The Gapu Photography account credits Manaswini Sahoo of Soul Of Odisha with a tala poda pitha preparation. Ripe palm fruit is its starting point.",
            "source_ids": [
              "food-tala-manaswini2018"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "origin",
        "title": "A taste with a season attached",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "That account places the fruit in a monsoon setting. It gives us a seasonal association to explore, rather than an exact availability calendar for every part of Odisha.",
            "source_ids": [
              "food-tala-manaswini2018"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          },
          {
            "text": "Ask a local cook when they look for the fruit and how they recognise it at the stage they want. Plan around their answer; a seasonal dish may be worth returning for.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "making",
        "title": "One fruit, more than one food",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "The featured account names tala poda pitha. Keep that specific preparation in view when exploring the wider name tala pitha; the page does not establish one method for every version.",
            "source_ids": [
              "food-tala-manaswini2018"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          },
          {
            "text": "Ripe-fruit preparations and palm-seed foods are separate stories. We are still documenting the precise seed stage and local usage of the name tala khaja; it should not be treated as another name for this cake.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "try",
        "title": "Let the maker introduce it",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Ask which preparation is available, what grains and other ingredients it contains, and when it was made. The picture cannot establish its recipe or suitability for dietary needs.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          },
          {
            "text": "Save the dish and the question for your journey. There is no verified outlet or cooking demonstration attached to this page. If a cook offers a story, make space for their own words and credit.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
